  "term": "NSF",
  "definition": "NSF stands for nasoseptal flap, a vascularized tissue flap taken from the septal lining of the nose and commonly used in endoscopic skull base surgery. It is attached by the posterior septal branch of the sphenopalatine artery and is used to help repair skull base defects and lower the risk of cerebrospinal fluid leakage.",
